    <h1>christopher j. joy</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">southeast asia &middot; researcher &middot; area studies</p>
  </div>
  <hr class="rule-accent" />

  <p>
    I'm Christopher — a Southeast Asia researcher and specialist with deep knowledge of the
    region's political economies, development trajectories, and state-society dynamics. I have
    spent significant portions of the last decade living and working in Southeast Asia and speak
    Vietnamese, Indonesian, and Thai. I hold advanced degrees in Southeast Asian Studies from
    <a href="https://www.soas.ac.uk/">SOAS, University of London</a> and Development Economics
    from <a href="http://www.city.ac.uk">City, University of London</a>. My research sits at the
    intersection of area studies and political economy, with sustained focus on gender empowerment,
    poverty reduction, and the dynamics of state capacity across the region.
  </p>

