  <h2>Regional Focus</h2>

  <p>
    My regional expertise centres on Việt Nam, Indonesia, and Thailand. I have lived and worked
    in Hà Nội, and have conducted research and fieldwork across the region. My analytical focus
    spans the political economies of ASEAN states, the developmental trajectories of rapidly
    growing economies, civil society and state-society relations, and the comparative study of
    gender outcomes and female empowerment within the region.
  </p>

  <h2>Background</h2>

  <p>
    Before returning to graduate school, I spent years working in Southeast Asia as a
    technology consultant and developer, operating primarily from Hà Nội and working with
    clients across the region. Prior to that, I built a career in software development and
    consulting in the United States, including at <a href="https://www.novachem.com">NOVA Chemicals</a>
    and through my own company. I now work as an economic researcher at
    <a href="https://www.alleghenyecon.com">Allegheny Economic Research</a>, applying quantitative
    methods to policy-relevant questions.
  </p>

